The client entrypoint belongs under `StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts`, not where it is now. Right now `default.project.json` maps `src/client` to `ReplicatedStorage.Client`, so `init.client.luau` becomes a LocalScript inside ReplicatedStorage. Roblox doesn't run LocalScripts there, so the `print("client")` never fires.

The server side is fine. `src/server` maps to `ServerScriptService.Server`, where a Script runs.

The fix is to change the mapping in `default.project.json`:

```json
"StarterPlayer": {
  "StarterPlayerScripts": { "Client": { "$path": "src/client" } }
}
```

Keep `Shared` in ReplicatedStorage, since both client and server need it. Client code that needs to be required from elsewhere should still live in `src/shared`.

I haven't changed anything since you asked a question. Should I make this edit? I'd also suggest one unrelated cleanup: the `Packages` mapping points at a `Packages` folder that doesn't exist yet, so Rojo will fail to build until you run Wally install or remove that line.
